-- BUILT (unit SRM16): dev run a5 (exit 0); the final-SHA rebuild in REPORT-SRM16.md is the only final evidence.
-- SCOPE (SRM16 audits).  (1) PREMISE TABLE of every new theorem (binders: index, binderInfo, name, Prop-or-data, type) EQUAL to `Tests/Compiler/Srm16AuditExpected.lean` and `scripts/srm16/PREMISES.txt`, one `S16THM` marker per theorem, literal count guard;
-- THREE negative fixtures (semantic ` ∧ True`, added data binder, reordered binders), each non-vacuous and rejected.  REGENERATION: `./.cluster/qbuild.sh build Tests.Compiler.Srm16AuditTest > LOG 2>&1; python3 scripts/srm16/gen_audit.py LOG`.
-- (2) INDEPENDENT EXPECTED STATEMENTS: `Tests/Compiler/Srm16ExpStmt.lean` is GENERATED by scripts/srm16/gen_exp.py from the SRM13 SOURCE statements only (explicit deletion/insertion list, printed by the script, reading only Tests/Compiler/Srm13ParentTest.lean);
-- each corollary / hO supplier is `isDefEq` to its expected form; a deliberately wrong form (hfit deleted) is rejected; the new residual Props are NOT defeq to the SRM13 premise `hrk` they replace (not relabellings).
-- (3) CLOSURE: standard axioms; forbidden old-form roots (with control); the SRM13 `_viaReset` theorem is in each corollary's closure.  NOT guaranteed: that the hypotheses hold for the machine's run.
set_option Elab.async false
set_option autoImplicit false
section
open Lean Elab Command Meta

namespace Tests.Compiler.Srm16AuditTest

/-- a hand-made MUTATION for the binder audit's control: a theorem whose single hypothesis IS its conclusion -/
theorem wrapper_mutation (p : Prop) (h : p) : p := h

